message.content:
I found one likely lesion. I'm not very confident in it: nothing on this radiograph shows a clearly defined radiolucency.

```json
{"lesions": [{"box": [0.243, 0.655, 0.283, 0.735], "pai": 3}]}
```

**The lesion:** it sits at the tips of the roots of the lower right molar that is tilted forward and holds up the bridge (the patient's right, on the left side of the image). Around the root tips the bone looks hazy and has lost some mineral, but the area has no sharp edge. That fits score 3, not 4 or 5.

**Teeth I checked and scored 1–2 (not lesions):**
- the two root-filled lower right premolars;
- the two root-filled lower left bridge supports;
- the root-filled upper right tooth with a post.

I judged this from enlarged, contrast-adjusted crops of the image. A periapical X-ray of the lower right molar would be needed to confirm the lesion and its grade.
